  "title": "USS Abraham Lincoln's Long Deployment and Health Concerns",
  "summary": "The USS Abraham Lincoln's prolonged deployment in the Middle East has led to reports of water shortages, plumbing issues, and mental health struggles among its crew, as highlighted by US Navy veterans and military health experts. The President has downplayed these concerns.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The USS Abraham Lincoln has been deployed in the Middle East for over a year, with reports of water shortages and mental health issues among its crew.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "US Navy veterans and military health experts have expressed concerns about the conditions aboard the Lincoln during its prolonged deployment.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The President has downplayed the concerns, citing the importance of the military and the need for continued operations against Iran.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
